{
  "id": "COMPOUND:27131 - PROTEIN:4718",
  "verbalization": "N,N-Dimethylacetamide is implicated in the target pathway leading to Myosin light chain kinase 3 through multiple indirect routes. The drug is shown to interact with receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta, which in turn is targeted by a complex molecule that ultimately directs the kinase to Myosin light chain kinase 3. Similarly, N,N-Dimethylacetamide is also shown to target Non-receptor tyrosine-protein kinase TNK1, which is further targeted by (2R)-pentan-2-ol, another molecule that also leads to Myosin light chain kinase 3. These pathways suggest that N,N-Dimethylacetamide may act as a modulator of signaling cascades involving tyrosine-protein kinases, potentially influencing the activity of Myosin light chain kinase 3. The evidence supports a mechanism where N,N-Dimethylacetamide may interact with tyrosine-protein kinases, possibly through a common intermediate, to influence the activity of Myosin light chain kinase 3. The relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, indicating a plausible biological role for N,N-Dimethylacetamide in modulating kinase activity.",
